@1 = ~Hostile Request~
@2 = ~An orog called Fistacio in the Docks district of Athkatla asked us to retrieve an amulet from a man called Pilther, in southern docks. He threatened that he will end my life if I don't abide by it. I need to think about how to proceed.~
@3 = ~We decided to side with Pilther and kill Fistacio. That way he will keep the amulet and flee the city, start his life fresh.~
@4 = ~We returned Fistacio's amulet to him. The orog kept his word, spared us, and left the Docks.~
@5 = ~We killed Fistacio and freed Pilther from his immediate pursuer. Pilther can now flee Athkatla and try to begin his life anew.~

// CotSC translation batch 5: dialogue text extracted; old entries preserved.
@6 = ~You're currently in the most dangerous part of town. Mark my words. Getting pickpocketed is on a daily basis around here.~
@7 = ~Hey, I recognise you. Weren't you the one who cleared Firewine ruins, near Gullykin?~
@8 = ~And what if I was?~
@9 = ~Nope. Wrong person.~
@10 = ~Whole village would not be existing if not for you. I hail from Gullykin. I saw you briefly when you visited our village. I thank you once again on behalf of my people. The village is at peace now. That fool, Jenkal did us all dirty. Here, take this. It's way overdue but I believe you should have it. For luck.~
@11 = ~Oh, you look strikingly similar. Forgive me for bothering you.~
@12 = ~I hope you have a nice day.~
@13 = ~Hold on, pearl. I have a business with you.~
@14 = ~Business, you say? I...~
@15 = ~Shhh. Hand over every single coin you have, immediately or suffer the consequences, pearl.~
@16 = ~Hah! You really think I'll part with my belongings because you tell me to?~
@17 = ~I have no gold.~
@18 = ~How about you turn around and go that way, and I'll go the opposite. I'll forget about this encounter and let you live.~
@19 = ~Frankly, yes. My victims end up poor or dead, pearl. It's best to be poor than dead. Well, in most cases. So, how is it going to be, pearl. Give me your gold?~
@20 = ~I have enough of this. Draw steel, witch!~
@21 = ~Okay, okay! Here is all my gold.~
@22 = ~I have no gold.~
@23 = ~Oh? Let me see. Stay still, close your eyes and put your hands up, pearl. It won't hurt... much.~
@24 = ~I like you, pearl. Too bad you won't live long enough for us to get to know each other better. You'd be flattered to know that you are my fortieth victim. Such a nice, round number, don't you think?~
@25 = ~How rude. I was beginning to respect you, pearl. Eh, I'm joking. I respect the money and nothing more. You made it personal now, so I shall kill you for both money and pleasure. Stay still, pearl.~
@26 = ~That's the spirit. See? That wasn't so difficult now, was it? Now go! And remember that these streets belong to Eulicia and her gang.~
@27 = ~Hey you!~
@28 = ~Me?~
@29 = ~Do you see anyone else in here? Of course I am talking to you. You will help me.~
@30 = ~I will...?~
@31 = ~You will. Docks area, south of here. There is a man down there called Pilther. He has an item on him. An amulet that he stole from me. You will get it back.~
@32 = ~And if I won't?~
@33 = ~What will be my reward?~
@34 = ~Then you shall die where you stand! I am not a patient individual, nor am I in a good mood. Do so, now!~
@35 = ~Okay, okay. Fine. I will do as you ask.~
@36 = ~I am not feeling generous toward those that threaten me. I think I'll teach you some manners.~
@37 = ~Reward? Don't make me laugh. Do you even know whom you face? I am Fistacio and I have power and authority around here. No one crosses me.~
@38 = ~I wouldn't make me mad if I were you. It would not end nicely for you. You! Make your choice and make it fast!~
@39 = ~Okay, okay. Fine. I will do as you ask.~
@40 = ~I am not feeling generous toward those that threaten me. I think I'll teach you some manners.~
@41 = ~Wise decision! South of here! Pilther! Go!~
@42 = ~Feel free to try. I'm always glad to murder some pieces of garbage that disrespect my authority.~
@43 = ~Do you have my amulet?~
@44 = ~Yes. Here.~
@45 = ~Not yet.~
@46 = ~We decided to kill you instead.~
@47 = ~Took your bloody time, didn't ya? You're lucky. Now, scram!~
@48 = ~Every second you protract, you make me angry. Get to it!~
@49 = ~Hah! Unwise!~
@50 = ~I haven't stolen anything! Now, go away.~
@51 = ~What do you want? I am no thief!~
@52 = ~I never said you are. I just want to talk.~
@53 = ~An aggressive orog told us a man named Pilther has his amulet. Is that you?~
@54 = ~I didn't say you are and I don't like your attitude so... bye.~
@55 = ~Talk? Ehm... all right. Let's... talk.~
@56 = ~An aggressive orog told us a man named Pilther has his amulet. Is that you?~
@57 = ~We've been told by some orog that you have an amulet, however we didn't like the tone of his voice. I'd rather hear your side of the story before I pick a side.~
@58 = ~Actually, I think I'll just kill you.~
@59 = ~N-no! My name... m-m-my name is Th-Theodor. Yeah. Theodor. No Pilther here. I think I would've known if my name was Pilther, but I'm not Pilther. What a stupid name! Phi! Pilther! Haha, hah... hah...~
@60 = ~Are you sure?~
@61 = ~Enough dumb games, Pilther. Tell me about the amulet.~
@62 = ~I... yeah. No. Yes! Oh, by Mask, no!~
@63 = ~I... it's not what you think. As cliché as it sounds, it really isn't what you think. My name is Pilther, yes! But I assure you I had the best intentions while stealing that amulet.~
@64 = ~The story is quite convoluted. The orog's name is Fistacio and he was hired as a bodyguard for Renal, who also happens to be my boss... previous boss. I deserted the guild and I was being hunted as punishment so I made an uneasy alliance with Renal instead. He offered me protection in exchange for service.~
@65 = ~I gladly agreed. I just didn't expect Renal plans to overthrow Mae'Var. The two share a conflict and I got caught up in the middle of it. I blame my own impulsivity for this. Fistacio was assigned as my temporary 'companion', if you will, but things went awry and during my infiltration mission I got caught.~
@66 = ~I took an easy way out. I stole what I thought was a priceless amulet, and fled. My plan was to sell it, gain enough gold to leave the town and start my life anew, maybe in a wilderness. Anywhere, just away from the guild.~
@67 = ~I can't go back to Renal cause I will be punished. I can't go back to Mae'Var because I will be killed. Escaping has now been made impossible because I am being tracked. Fistacio already got appointed as my executioner, if the word on the street is correct. I keep a low profile here, whilst Fistacio just plays with his food. Me!~
@68 = ~I want to start over clean. I will abandon dishonesty and my current lifestyle and make healthier choices, but I need to survive first and the whole district is against me. If you'd help me, I can leave my thief life behind.~
@69 = ~If you want me to, I can remove Fistacio.~
@70 = ~Do you want me to talk to any guild masters to rid you of your offences?~
@71 = ~The deal was I get the amulet. As touching as your story was, I think I'll just kill you.~
@72 = ~Both Renal and Mae'Var have more pressing matters to attend to currently, so even though I am on their radar I must stick to the shadows. If you eliminate that blasted orog, I can sneak out of the district and sell the amulet. Money it brings will be enough to cover my departure. Come back to me, when it's done.~
@73 = ~It won't grant my amnesty, no doubt. As a matter of fact, it will plunge me deeper into this mess. So no, that isn't ideal.~
@74 = ~If you want me to, I can remove Fistacio.~
@75 = ~The deal was I get the amulet. As touching as your story was, I think I'll just kill you.~
@76 = ~You won't take me alive!~
@77 = ~To think I swallowed that crap about you considering helping me. You won't take me alive!~
@78 = ~Come back to me when Fistacio is dead. I can't risk showing myself while he's still out there.~
@79 = ~Is it done?~
@80 = ~Yes. Fistacio won't trouble you any longer. You can leave.~
@81 = ~Fabulous! Then I can take my leave and get away from this city. I can't offer you anything as a reward as I possess nothing but the amulet, but I will remember you fondly. Doesn't that matter the most?~
@82 = ~Looking for potions? I have a few bottles worth browsing.~
@83 = ~Show me what you have.~
@84 = ~Not right now.~
@85 = ~I don't like the look of you. Have you come back to pledge your loyalty to Renal yet again?~
@86 = ~Brave of you to walk amongst thieves. Some of these buildings are their hideout.~
@87 = ~Just stick to your business and don't put yourself in a bigger debt.~
@88 = ~Me be on my shift. You don't talk to me.~
@89 = ~Life of a fisherman is simple. You take a rod, you clear your mind and relax. Try it sometime.~
@90 = ~Unless you want a bloodshed, don't bother me.~
@91 = ~I-I... I didn't mean anything by it. Just leave me alone.~
@92 = ~Me work hard. See?~
@93 = ~Work, work and work. My days are tough. Honest work is fair, master says.~
@94 = ~Ergh not lazy. Ergh is on a break. Don't yell at Ergh.~
@95 = ~Speak to Thumb, not me. I am just here to keep the peace.~
@96 = ~Could you stomp any harder? My head is about to explode from the sheer noise.~
@97 = ~Humility. I expect humility.~
@98 = ~This Orog gives me a bad feeling, <CHARNAME>. I think we should leave or... lie that we undertake his quest and just get away.~
@99 = ~He seems sincere... and honest. I think we should help him.~
@100 = ~If you want me to, I can remove Fistacio.~
@101 = ~Do you want me to talk to any guild masters to rid you of your offences?~
@102 = ~The deal was I get the amulet. As touching as your story was, I think I'll just kill you.~
@103 = ~Boo takes no orders from self-righteous imbeciles such as you! I say we put him in his place!~
@104 = ~Happy to see you too, Bonzo. Let my business remain mine. We wouldn't want my companions to hear about your 'from behind' incident, would we?~
@105 = ~Another loser who just craves the attention of my blade.~
@106 = ~This is a public space. I really don't get what you expect.~
